From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:33:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the video call media path against live WhatsApp clients

Changes made while bringing up 1:1 video calls between a webOS device
and the official Android client, kept where upstream does not already
do the same:

- answer relaylatency probes for calls we place, not only for calls we
  receive; the event fires in both directions
- send an ICE Binding Request carrying the relay token before DTLS, and
  close the relay channel as soon as the call context ends instead of
  leaking its socket and keep-alive
- use one RTCP CNAME for audio and video, send the first sender report
  as soon as the relay allocation succeeds, and keep sending PLI and FIR
  at the peer's video SSRC until (and briefly after) its first frame
- send dependent frames from the start instead of holding them back
  until an IDR, which starved the outgoing stream for whole calls
- advertise the video capability and screen size live clients offer
- log relay ALLOCATE-SUCCESS, ALLOCATE-ERROR and consent PONG

Upstream has since done the RTP header, H.264 access unit packetisation
and loss-aware access unit assembly this patch used to carry, and
accepts a peer's video upgrade through Call.AcceptVideo(), so those
parts are gone. The sender reports keep upstream's reception reports.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
